<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teatro Farnese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Teatro Farnese is a wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> inside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-della-pilotta">Palazzo della Pilotta</a> in Parma, built in 1618 for Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranuccio-i-farnese-duke-of-parma">Ranuccio I Farnese</a> to designs by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-battista-aleotti">Giovanni Battista Aleotti</a>. Its permanent proscenium arch makes it one of the earliest theatres of its kind. Largely destroyed by bombing in 1944, it was rebuilt after the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teatro-farnese.jpg" alt="Teatro Farnese" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: www.bestofcinqueterre.com · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parma-teatro-farnese-in-national-gallery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
